    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{1}{4}\cdot 1^{3}\cdot 4-\frac{1}{8}\cdot 1^{5}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x = -1</m> and <m>x = 0</m>,
below by <m>y = -\sqrt{4 - x^2}</m> and above by <m>y = 0</m>.  The
correct region is therefore 3.
Evaluating the integral, we have
<me>\int_{-1}^{0}\int_{-\sqrt{4-x^{2}}}^{0} 1 x y\, dy dx =
    \int_{-1}^{0} \frac{1}{2}\, x \, y^{2}\bigg|_{-\sqrt{4-x^{2}}}^{0} dx
    = \int_{-1}^{0} -\frac{1}{2} x (4 - x^2)\,dx</me>
<me>-\frac{1}{2}\int_{-1}^{0} 4 x - x^{3}\, dx
    = -\frac{1}{2}\left( 4(\frac12)(x^2) - (\frac14)(x^4)\right)\bigg|_{-1}^{0}</me>
<me>= \frac{1}{4}\,4 - \frac{1}{8} = \frac{7}{8}.</me>



</solution>
